# Root .gitignore: what this repository refuses to track.
#
# Scoped deliberately narrow. `.harnx/.gitignore` and `.worktrees/.gitignore`
# already cover what belongs to those directories, and repeating their entries
# here would create two places to change one rule. This file is for what has no
# directory of its own.

# Tool caches and state, none of which is reproducible from the tree and all of
# which is derived. `mise.toml` pins the versions; nothing here is an input.
.mise/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor and OS droppings. Not tracked, and equally not a reason for anybody
# else to see a diff.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Secrets, by shape rather than by name. Nothing in this repository should ever
# hold one, and `gitleaks` runs over the history as a real gate rather than
# relying on this list. This is the earlier of the two lines of defence: it
# stops the accident, while gitleaks catches what got past it.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
